    "description": "Finally is the default clause of a try-catch expression. It is run after all the catch clauses have been called.\n\nFinally is run every time after a try, with or without any catch clause. It is also run before the return expression, if any.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    try {\n        doSomething();\n    } catch (\\Exception $e) {\n        print \"An exception was raised and caught\";\n    } finally {\n        print \"Finally\\n\";\n    }\n\n?>",
